/// rcdzc RESOLVE BUG (not a reader bug) — a user function named `quote` (or any def whose arena head
/// after the `def` is the name `quote`) has its BODY resolved as a QUASIQUOTE context: an identifier in
/// the body becomes a reified symbol instead of a variable reference, so a reference to the function's
/// own PARAMETER is reported CDZ0101 "unbound name".
///
///   def quote(x) = x + 2        →  arena (def (quote x) (+ x 2))   [reader output is CORRECT]
///   → error CDZ0101 "unbound name `x`" at the body's `x`
///
/// ROOT CAUSE: resolve.rs:380 dispatches `Some("quote") => resolve_quote(db, id)` on ANY node whose
/// head_name is "quote" — including the def SIGNATURE/BODY of a user function named `quote`. The
/// parameter `x` binds in the signature, but the body `(+ x 2)` is resolved under the quote special-case
/// (or the def routes through resolve_quote), so `x` never looks up the bound param.
///
/// NOT A CADENZA-SYNTAX READER BUG (v-syntax verified): the SAME failure occurs feeding the s-expr
/// `(def (quote x) (+ x 2))` directly (bypassing the ML reader). Both surfaces produce the correct
/// arena; the fault is purely at resolve. Trigger is the BODY referencing a bound name: `def quote(x) =
/// 99` only warns "unused param" (no error), `def quote(x) = x + 2` errors on `x`.
///
/// SUGGESTED FIX (rcdzc territory): the `Some("quote")` dispatch at resolve.rs:380 must only fire for a
/// genuine quasiquote FORM, not for a def whose name happens to be `quote` — i.e. gate the special-case
/// so a `(def (quote …) …)` (a definition of a function NAMED quote) resolves as an ordinary def. The
/// compound-ctor heads (`list`/`tuple`/`record`/`map`) already avoid this via the reserved-string-vs-name
/// distinction; `quote`/`bin`/`match`/etc. as user def names need the same treatment. (`bin` may share
/// the bug via resolve.rs:383 `Some("bin") => resolve_bin`; confirm.)
///
/// This file DECLINES to compile today (the bug). It becomes a passing/witness case once fixed.
def quote(x: Int64) = x + 2

export { quote }

/// RESOLVED 2026-07-15 (trunk@f9a316eae, fix f9a316eae / PR #406): a user (def (quote x) …) no longer hijacked. ROOT was NOT resolve.rs:380 head-dispatch (v-syntax hypothesis) but quote::reify_quotes — a LOAD-time shape pre-pass rewrote (quote x) → (Ast.Name x) before build_scope_binders, erasing the param. Fix: reify_quotes skips def-sig/fn-param lists. Witness in 12-metaprogramming.sexp. bin/if/match never affected.
